{"id":"mahabharata-5-056","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · Who will fight whom","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya lists the Pandava warriors and the Kaurava foes each has chosen: Bhishma for Shikhandin, Drona for Dhrishtadyumna, Karna for Arjuna, Duryodhana and his brothers for Bhima. Duryodhana boasts that his warriors will defeat them, but Dhritarashtra warns that Arjuna's chariot, built by the gods, cannot be conquered by men.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವವೀರರನ್ನೂ ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಬ್ಬರೂ ಆರಿಸಿದ ಕೌರವ ಶತ್ರುಗಳನ್ನೂ ಸಂಜಯನು ಪಟ್ಟಿಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಶಿಖಂಡಿಗೆ ಭೀಷ್ಮ, ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನಿಗೆ ದ್ರೋಣ, ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಕರ್ಣ, ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಮತ್ತು ಸಹೋದರರು. ತನ್ನ ವೀರರು ಅವರನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸುವರೆಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಬಡಾಯಿ ಕೊಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ದೇವತೆಗಳು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿದ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ರಥವನ್ನು ಮನುಷ್ಯರು ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾರರು ಎಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सञ्जय पाण्डव योद्धाओं और प्रत्येक द्वारा चुने गए कौरव शत्रुओं की सूची देते हैं: शिखण्डी के लिए भीष्म, धृष्टद्युम्न के लिए द्रोण, अर्जुन के लिए कर्ण, भीम के लिए दुर्योधन और उसके भाई। दुर्योधन डींग मारता है कि उसके योद्धा उन्हें हरा देंगे, पर धृतराष्ट्र चेताते हैं कि देवताओं द्वारा बनाया अर्जुन का रथ मनुष्यों से जीता नहीं जा सकता।","te":"పాండవవీరులను, ఒక్కొక్కరూ ఎంచుకున్న కౌరవ శత్రువులను సంజయుడు జాబితా చేస్తాడు: శిఖండికి భీష్ముడు, ధృష్టద్యుమ్నునికి ద్రోణుడు, అర్జునునికి కర్ణుడు, భీమునికి దుర్యోధనుడు, సోదరులు. తన వీరులు వారిని ఓడిస్తారని దుర్యోధనుడు గొప్పలు చెబుతాడు, కానీ దేవతలు నిర్మించిన అర్జునుని రథాన్ని మనుషులు జయించలేరని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவ வீரர்களையும் ஒவ்வொருவரும் தேர்ந்தெடுத்த கௌரவப் பகைவர்களையும் ஸஞ்ஜயன் பட்டியலிடுகிறான்: ஶிகண்டிக்குப் பீஷ்மர், த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனுக்கு த்ரோணர், அர்ஜுனனுக்குக் கர்ணன், பீமனுக்குத் துரியோதனனும் சகோதரர்களும். தன் வீரர்கள் அவர்களை வெல்வார்கள் என்று துரியோதனன் வீம்பு பேச, தேவர்கள் அமைத்த அர்ஜுனனின் தேரை மனிதர்களால் வெல்ல முடியாது என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் எச்சரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവയോദ്ധാക്കളെയും അവരുടെ കൗരവ എതിരാളികളെയും സഞ്ജയൻ പട്ടികപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു: ശിഖണ്ഡിക്കെതിരെ ഭീഷ്മർ, ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനെതിരെ ദ്രോണർ, അർജുനനെതിരെ കർണ്ണൻ, ഭീമനെതിരെ ദുര്യോധനനും സഹോദരന്മാരും. തന്റെ യോദ്ധാക്കൾ അവരെ തോൽപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ വീമ്പിളക്കുന്നു; എന്നാൽ ദേവന്മാർ നിർമ്മിച്ച അർജുനന്റെ രഥത്തെ മനുഷ്യർക്ക് ജയിക്കാനാകില്ലെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"यानसंधिपर्व","titleEn":"Yanasandhi Parva (Debate on peace)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कांस्तत्र संजयापश्यः प्रत्यर्थेन समागतान् ।\nये योत्स्यन्ते पाण्डवार्थे पुत्रस्य मम वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, whom did you see gathered on the other side, who will fight my son's army for the Pandavas' sake?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"मुख्यमन्धकवृष्णीनामपश्यं कृष्णमागतम् ।\nचेकितानं च तत्रैव युयुधानं च सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw Krishna, chief of the Andhakas and Vrishnis, arrive, and with him Chekitana and Yuyudhana Satyaki."}},{"n":3,"text":"पृथगक्षौहिणीभ्यां तौ पाण्डवानभिसंश्रितौ ।\nमहारथौ समाख्यातावुभौ पुरुषमानिनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each with a separate akshauhini, those two great chariot-warriors, both proud men, have joined the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"अक्षौहिण्याथ पाञ्चाल्यो दशभिस्तनयैर्वृतः ।\nसत्यजित्प्रमुखैर्वीरैर्धृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchala king Drupada, surrounded by ten sons led by heroes such as Satyajit with Dhrishtadyumna at their head, with one akshauhini,"}},{"n":5,"text":"द्रुपदो वर्धयन्मानं शिखण्डिपरिपालितः ।\nउपायात्सर्वसैन्यानां प्रतिच्छाद्य तदा वपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"protected by Shikhandi, increasing his honour, came, covering his own form among all the armies."}},{"n":6,"text":"विराटः सह पुत्राभ्यां शङ्खेनैवोत्तरेण च ।\nसूर्यदत्तादिभिर्वीरैर्मदिराश्वपुरोगमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata with his two sons Shankha and Uttara, with heroes led by Suryadatta and Madirashva,"}},{"n":7,"text":"सहितः पृथिवीपालो भ्रातृभिस्तनयैस्तथा ।\nअक्षौहिण्यैव सैन्यस्य वृतः पार्थं समाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the earth-lord with his brothers and sons, surrounded by one akshauhini of troops, has joined Partha."}},{"n":8,"text":"जारासंधिर्मागधश्च धृष्टकेतुश्च चेदिराट् ।\nपृथक्पृथगनुप्राप्तौ पृथगक्षौहिणीवृतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jarasandha's son of Magadha and Dhrishtaketu the Chedi king came, each separately, each with a separate akshauhini."}},{"n":9,"text":"केकया भ्रातरः पञ्च सर्वे लोहितकध्वजाः ।\nअक्षौहिणीपरिवृताः पाण्डवानभिसंश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Kekaya brothers, all with red banners, surrounded by an akshauhini, have joined the Pandavas."}},{"n":10,"text":"एतानेतावतस्तत्र यानपश्यं समागतान् ।\nये पाण्डवार्थे योत्स्यन्ति धार्तराष्ट्रस्य वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are all I saw gathered there, who will fight Dhritarashtra's army for the Pandavas."}},{"n":11,"text":"यो वेद मानुषं व्यूहं दैवं गान्धर्वमासुरम् ।\nस तस्य सेनाप्रमुखे धृष्टद्युम्नो महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-minded Dhrishtadyumna, who knows the human, divine, gandharva and asura formations, is at the front of their army."}},{"n":12,"text":"भीष्मः शांतनवो राजन्भागः कॢप्तः शिखण्डिनः ।\nतं विराटोऽनु संयाता सह मत्स्यैः प्रहारिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Shantanu's son, king, is assigned to Shikhandi, and Virata with the striking Matsyas follows him."}},{"n":13,"text":"ज्येष्ठस्य पाण्डुपुत्रस्य भागो मद्राधिपो बली ।\nतौ तु तत्राब्रुवन्केचिद्विषमौ नो मताविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The share of the eldest Pandava is the mighty king of Madra; some there said the two were not evenly matched."}},{"n":14,"text":"दुर्योधनः सहसुतः सार्धं भ्रातृशतेन च ।\nप्राच्याश्च दाक्षिणात्याश्च भीमसेनस्य भागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana with his sons and a hundred brothers, and the easterners and southerners, fall to Bhimasena's share."}},{"n":15,"text":"अर्जुनस्य तु भागेन कर्णो वैकर्तनो मतः ।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सैन्धवश्च जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To Arjuna's share are assigned Karna Vaikartana, Ashvatthama, Vikarna and Jayadratha of the Sindhus."}},{"n":16,"text":"अशक्याश्चैव ये केचित्पृथिव्यां शूरमानिनः ।\nसर्वांस्तानर्जुनः पार्थः कल्पयामास भागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever proud heroes on earth cannot be overcome, Partha Arjuna has assigned all of them to himself."}},{"n":17,"text":"महेष्वासा राजपुत्रा भ्रातरः पञ्च केकयाः ।\nकेकयानेव भागेन कृत्वा योत्स्यन्ति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Kekaya brothers, princes and great archers, will fight in battle taking the Kekayas as their share."}},{"n":18,"text":"तेषामेव कृतो भागो मालवाः शाल्वकेकयाः ।\nत्रिगर्तानां च द्वौ मुख्यौ यौ तौ संशप्तकाविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For them also are assigned the Malavas, Shalvas and Kekayas, and the two chief Trigartas called Samshaptakas."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्योधनसुताः सर्वे तथा दुःशासनस्य च ।\nसौभद्रेण कृतो भागो राजा चैव बृहद्बलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the sons of Duryodhana and of Duhshasana, and King Brihadbala, are assigned to Subhadra's son."}},{"n":20,"text":"द्रौपदेया महेष्वासाः सुवर्णविकृतध्वजाः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नमुखा द्रोणमभियास्यन्ति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi's sons, great archers with golden-fashioned banners, led by Dhrishtadyumna, will go against Drona, Bharata."}},{"n":21,"text":"चेकितानः सोमदत्तं द्वैरथे योद्धुमिच्छति ।\nभोजं तु कृतवर्माणं युयुधानो युयुत्सति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chekitana wants to fight Somadatta in a duel; Yuyudhana seeks the Bhoja Kritavarma."}},{"n":22,"text":"सहदेवस्तु माद्रेयः शूरः संक्रन्दनो युधि ।\nस्वमंशं कल्पयामास श्यालं ते सुबलात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave Sahadeva, Madri's son, a challenger in battle, has marked as his share your wife's brother, Subala's son Shakuni."}},{"n":23,"text":"उलूकं चापि कैतव्यं ये च सारस्वता गणाः ।\nनकुलः कल्पयामास भागं माद्रवतीसुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, Madravati's son, has marked as his share Uluka Kaitavya and the Sarasvata troops."}},{"n":24,"text":"ये चान्ये पार्थिवा राजन्प्रत्युद्यास्यन्ति संयुगे ।\nसमाह्वानेन तांश्चापि पाण्डुपुत्रा अकल्पयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever other kings will come against them in battle, the sons of Pandu have assigned them by challenge."}},{"n":25,"text":"एवमेषामनीकानि प्रविभक्तानि भागशः ।\nयत्ते कार्यं सपुत्रस्य क्रियतां तदकालिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So their armies are divided by shares; do now whatever must be done by you and your sons, and without delay."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"न सन्ति सर्वे पुत्रा मे मूढा दुर्द्यूतदेविनः ।\nयेषां युद्धं बलवता भीमेन रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All my sons are fools who play at bad dice, whose war is with mighty Bhima at the head of the battle."}},{"n":27,"text":"राजानः पार्थिवाः सर्वे प्रोक्षिताः कालधर्मणा ।\nगाण्डीवाग्निं प्रवेक्ष्यन्ति पतङ्गा इव पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings are sprinkled by the law of Time; they will enter the Gandiva fire like moths into a flame."}},{"n":28,"text":"विद्रुतां वाहिनीं मन्ये कृतवैरैर्महात्मभिः ।\nतां रणे केऽनुयास्यन्ति प्रभग्नां पाण्डवैर्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think my army is already routed by those great ones who have taken up the feud; who will follow it, broken in battle by the Pandavas?"}},{"n":29,"text":"सर्वे ह्यतिरथाः शूराः कीर्तिमन्तः प्रतापिनः ।\nसूर्यपावकयोस्तुल्यास्तेजसा समितिंजयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them are heroes, great fighters, famous and mighty, equal to sun and fire in splendour, winners in battle,"}},{"n":30,"text":"येषां युधिष्ठिरो नेता गोप्ता च मधुसूदनः ।\nयोधौ च पाण्डवौ वीरौ सव्यसाचिवृकोदरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"with Yudhishthira as leader and Madhusudana as protector, with the two Pandava warriors Savyasachin and Vrikodara,"}},{"n":31,"text":"नकुलः सहदेवश्च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nसात्यकिर्द्रुपदश्चैव धृष्टद्युम्नस्य चात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, Sahadeva, Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata, Satyaki, Drupada, and Dhrishtadyumna's son,"}},{"n":32,"text":"उत्तमौजाश्च पाञ्चाल्यो युधामन्युश्च दुर्जयः ।\nशिखण्डी क्षत्रदेवश्च तथा वैराटिरुत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Uttamaujas the Panchala, unconquerable Yudhamanyu, Shikhandi, Kshatradeva and Uttara of Virata,"}},{"n":33,"text":"काशयश्चेदयश्चैव मत्स्याः सर्वे च सृञ्जयाः ।\nविराटपुत्रो बभ्रुश्च पाञ्चालाश्च प्रभद्रकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Kashis, Chedis, Matsyas and all Srinjayas, Virata's son Babhru, the Panchalas and Prabhadrakas,"}},{"n":34,"text":"येषामिन्द्रोऽप्यकामानां न हरेत्पृथिवीमिमाम् ।\nवीराणां रणधीराणां ये भिन्द्युः पर्वतानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"heroes steady in war, who could split mountains, from whom even Indra could not take this earth against their will."}},{"n":35,"text":"तान्सर्वान्गुणसंपन्नानमनुष्यप्रतापिनः ।\nक्रोशतो मम दुष्पुत्रो योद्धुमिच्छति संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these virtuous men of superhuman might: while I cry out, my evil son wishes to fight them, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"उभौ स्व एकजातीयौ तथोभौ भूमिगोचरौ ।\nअथ कस्मात्पाण्डवानामेकतो मन्यसे जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We two are of one kind, both walk the earth; why then do you think victory lies with the Pandavas alone?"}},{"n":37,"text":"पितामहं च द्रोणं च कृपं कर्णं च दुर्जयम् ।\nजयद्रथं सोमदत्तमश्वत्थामानमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandfather, Drona, Kripa, unconquerable Karna, Jayadratha, Somadatta and Ashvatthama,"}},{"n":38,"text":"सुचेतसो महेष्वासानिन्द्रोऽपि सहितोऽमरैः ।\nअशक्तः समरे जेतुं किं पुनस्तात पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"all great archers of good mind: even Indra with the immortals could not defeat them in battle, so what of the Pandavas, father?"}},{"n":39,"text":"सर्वा च पृथिवी सृष्टा मदर्थे तात पाण्डवान् ।\nआर्यान्धृतिमतः शूरानग्निकल्पान्प्रबाधितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole earth has been made for me to put down the Pandavas, noble, steady, brave, and like fire."}},{"n":40,"text":"न मामकान्पाण्डवास्ते समर्थाः प्रतिवीक्षितुम् ।\nपराक्रान्तो ह्यहं पाण्डून्सपुत्रान्योद्धुमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Pandavas cannot even look at my men; I have the strength to fight the Pandavas and their sons in battle."}},{"n":41,"text":"मत्प्रियं पार्थिवाः सर्वे ये चिकीर्षन्ति भारत ।\nते तानावारयिष्यन्ति ऐणेयानिव तन्तुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"All kings who wish to please me will hold them back like deer with a string."}},{"n":42,"text":"महता रथवंशेन शरजालैश्च मामकैः ।\nअभिद्रुता भविष्यन्ति पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas with the Pandavas will be assailed by a great line of chariots and my nets of arrows."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"उन्मत्त इव मे पुत्रो विलपत्येष संजय ।\nन हि शक्तो युधा जेतुं धर्मराजं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son laments like a madman, Sanjaya; he cannot defeat Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, in battle."}},{"n":44,"text":"जानाति हि सदा भीष्मः पाण्डवानां यशस्विनाम् ।\nबलवत्तां सपुत्राणां धर्मज्ञानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma always knows the strength of the glorious Pandavas, righteous and great-souled, with their sons."}},{"n":45,"text":"यतो नारोचयमहं विग्रहं तैर्महात्मभिः ।\nकिं तु संजय मे ब्रूहि पुनस्तेषां विचेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is why I did not approve of war with those great souls. But tell me again, Sanjaya, what they are doing."}},{"n":46,"text":"कस्तांस्तरस्विनो भूयः संदीपयति पाण्डवान् ।\nअर्चिष्मतो महेष्वासान्हविषा पावकानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who keeps kindling those swift, blazing great archers, the Pandavas, like fires with oblation?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":47,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः सदैवैतान्संदीपयति भारत ।\nयुध्यध्वमिति मा भैष्ट युद्धाद्भरतसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna always kindles them, Bharata: \"Fight, do not fear battle, best of Bharatas.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"ये केचित्पार्थिवास्तत्र धार्तराष्ट्रेण संवृताः ।\nयुद्धे समागमिष्यन्ति तुमुले कवचह्रदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever kings come together in the tumultuous battle, in the lake of armour, led by Dhritarashtra's son,"}},{"n":49,"text":"तान्सर्वानाहवे क्रुद्धान्सानुबन्धान्समागतान् ।\nअहमेकः समादास्ये तिमिर्मत्स्यानिवौदकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I alone shall take them all, angry in battle with their kin, as a whale takes small fish."}},{"n":50,"text":"भीष्मं द्रोणं कृपं कर्णं द्रौणिं शल्यं सुयोधनम् ।\nएतांश्चापि निरोत्स्यामि वेलेव मकरालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall hold back Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Karna, Drona's son, Shalya and Suyodhana as the shore holds the sea.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"तथा ब्रुवाणं धर्मात्मा प्राह राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nतव धैर्यं च वीर्यं च पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सह ।\nसर्वे समधिरूढाः स्म संग्रामान्नः समुद्धर ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he spoke so, the righteous king Yudhishthira said: \"Your steadiness and valour, with the Panchalas and Pandavas, all rest on us; save us from the battle."}},{"n":52,"text":"जानामि त्वां महाबाहो क्षत्रधर्मे व्यवस्थितम् ।\nसमर्थमेकं पर्याप्तं कौरवाणां युयुत्सताम् ।\nभवता यद्विधातव्यं तन्नः श्रेयः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know you, mighty-armed, are set in the kshatriya's duty and capable alone against the Kauravas who want battle; what you must do, scorcher of foes, is best for us."}},{"n":53,"text":"संग्रामादपयातानां भग्नानां शरणैषिणाम् ।\nपौरुषं दर्शयञ्शूरो यस्तिष्ठेदग्रतः पुमान् ।\nक्रीणीयात्तं सहस्रेण नीतिमन्नाम तत्पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brave man who shows his manhood and stands at the front for those who flee the battle, broken and seeking refuge, one should buy for a thousand; that is called good policy.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"स त्वं शूरश्च वीरश्च विक्रान्तश्च नरर्षभ ।\nभयार्तानां परित्राता संयुगेषु न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are brave and heroic and full of valour, bull among men; beyond doubt you are the protector of the frightened in battles.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति कौन्तेये धर्मात्मनि युधिष्ठिरे ।\nधृष्टद्युम्न उवाचेदं मां वचो गतसाध्वसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As righteous Yudhishthira, Kunti's son, said this, Dhrishtadyumna, free of fear, spoke these words to me:"}},{"n":56,"text":"सर्वाञ्जनपदान्सूत योधा दुर्योधनस्य ये ।\nसबाह्लीकान्कुरून्ब्रूयाः प्रातिपेयाञ्शरद्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, tell all the countries and Duryodhana's warriors, the Kurus with the Bahlikas, the Pratipeyas, and Sharadvata,"}},{"n":57,"text":"सूतपुत्रं तथा द्रोणं सहपुत्रं जयद्रथम् ।\nदुःशासनं विकर्णं च तथा दुर्योधनं नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the charioteer's son, Drona with his son, Jayadratha, Duhshasana, Vikarna and King Duryodhana,"}},{"n":58,"text":"भीष्मं चैव ब्रूहि गत्वा त्वमाशु\nयुधिष्ठिरं साधुनैवाभ्युपेत ।\nमा वो वधीदर्जुनो देवगुप्तः\nक्षिप्रं याचध्वं पाण्डवं लोकवीरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and go quickly to Bhishma and say: 'Approach Yudhishthira properly; let Arjuna, guarded by the gods, not kill you. Quickly beg the Pandava, hero of the world."}},{"n":59,"text":"नैतादृशो हि योधोऽस्ति पृथिव्यामिह कश्चन ।\nयथाविधः सव्यसाची पाण्डवः शस्त्रवित्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no warrior like Savyasachin, the Pandava, best of weapon-knowers, anywhere on earth."}},{"n":60,"text":"देवैर्हि संभृतो दिव्यो रथो गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nन स जेयो मनुष्येण मा स्म कृध्वं मनो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The divine chariot of the Gandiva bowman was prepared by the gods; he cannot be defeated by a man; do not set your minds to fight.'\""}}]}]}